      "## list\n\n`client.accounts.list(created_at?: { after?: string; before?: string; on_or_after?: string; on_or_before?: string; }, cursor?: string, entity_id?: string, idempotency_key?: string, informational_entity_id?: string, limit?: number, program_id?: string, status?: { in?: 'closed' | 'open'[]; }): { data: account[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n\n**get** `/accounts`\n\nList Accounts\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `created_at?: { after?: string; before?: string; on_or_after?: string; on_or_before?: string; }`\n  - `after?: string`\n    Return results after this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n  - `before?: string`\n    Return results before this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n  - `on_or_after?: string`\n    Return results on or after this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n  - `on_or_before?: string`\n    Return results on or before this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n\n- `cursor?: string`\n  Return the page of entries after this one.\n\n- `entity_id?: string`\n  Filter Accounts for those belonging to the specified Entity.\n\n- `idempotency_key?: string`\n  Filter records to the one with the specified `idempotency_key` you chose for that object. This value is unique across Increase and is used to ensure that a request is only processed once. Learn more about [idempotency](https://increase.com/documentation/idempotency-keys).\n\n- `informational_entity_id?: string`\n  Filter Accounts for those belonging to the specified Entity as informational.\n\n- `limit?: number`\n  Limit the size of the list that is returned. The default (and maximum) is 100 objects.\n\n- `program_id?: string`\n  Filter Accounts for those in a specific Program.\n\n- `status?: { in?: 'closed' | 'open'[]; }`\n  - `in?: 'closed' | 'open'[]`\n    Filter Accounts for those with the specified status. For GET requests, this should be encoded as a comma-delimited string, such as `?in=one,two,three`.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ data: { id: string; account_revenue_rate: string; bank: 'core_bank' | 'first_internet_bank' | 'grasshopper_bank'; closed_at: string; created_at: string; currency: 'USD'; entity_id: string; funding: 'loan' | 'deposits'; idempotency_key: string; informational_entity_id: string; interest_accrued: string; interest_accrued_at: string; interest_rate: string; loan: object; name: string; program_id: string; status: 'closed' | 'open'; type: 'account'; }[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n  A list of Account objects.\n\n  - `data: { id: string; account_revenue_rate: string; bank: 'core_bank' | 'first_internet_bank' | 'grasshopper_bank'; closed_at: string; created_at: string; currency: 'USD'; entity_id: string; funding: 'loan' | 'deposits'; idempotency_key: string; informational_entity_id: string; interest_accrued: string; interest_accrued_at: string; interest_rate: string; loan: { credit_limit: number; grace_period_days: number; maturity_date: string; statement_day_of_month: number; statement_payment_type: 'balance' | 'interest_until_maturity'; }; name: string; program_id: string; status: 'closed' | 'open'; type: 'account'; }[]`\n  - `next_cursor: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport YolkenIncreaseTest from 'yolken-increase-test';\n\nconst client = new YolkenIncreaseTest();\n\nconst accounts = await client.accounts.list();\n\nconsole.log(accounts);\n```",
