    markdown:
      "## create\n\n`client.accounts.create(name: string, entity_id?: string, funding?: 'loan' | 'deposits', informational_entity_id?: string, loan?: { credit_limit: number; grace_period_days: number; statement_day_of_month: number; statement_payment_type: 'balance' | 'interest_until_maturity'; maturity_date?: string; }, program_id?: string): { id: string; account_revenue_rate: string; bank: 'core_bank' | 'first_internet_bank' | 'grasshopper_bank'; closed_at: string; created_at: string; currency: 'USD'; entity_id: string; funding: 'loan' | 'deposits'; idempotency_key: string; informational_entity_id: string; interest_accrued: string; interest_accrued_at: string; interest_rate: string; loan: object; name: string; program_id: string; status: 'closed' | 'open'; type: 'account'; }`\n\n**post** `/accounts`\n\nCreate an Account\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `name: string`\n  The name you choose for the Account.\n\n- `entity_id?: string`\n  The identifier for the Entity that will own the Account.\n\n- `funding?: 'loan' | 'deposits'`\n  Whether the Account is funded by a loan or by deposits.\n\n- `loan` - An account funded by a loan. Before opening a loan account, contact support@increase.com to set up a loan program.\n- `deposits` - An account funded by deposits.\n\n- `informational_entity_id?: string`\n  The identifier of an Entity that, while not owning the Account, is associated with its activity. This is generally the beneficiary of the funds.\n\n- `loan?: { credit_limit: number; grace_period_days: number; statement_day_of_month: number; statement_payment_type: 'balance' | 'interest_until_maturity'; maturity_date?: string; }`\n  The loan details for the account.\n  - `credit_limit: number`\n    The maximum amount of money that can be drawn from the Account.\n  - `grace_period_days: number`\n    The number of days after the statement date that the Account can be past due before being considered delinquent.\n  - `statement_day_of_month: number`\n    The day of the month on which the loan statement is generated.\n  - `statement_payment_type: 'balance' | 'interest_until_maturity'`\n    The type of statement payment for the account.\n\n- `balance` - The borrower must pay the full balance of the loan at the end of the statement period.\n- `interest_until_maturity` - The borrower must pay the accrued interest at the end of the statement period.\n  - `maturity_date?: string`\n    The date on which the loan matures.\n\n- `program_id?: string`\n  The identifier for the Program that this Account falls under. Required if you operate more than one Program.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id: string; account_revenue_rate: string; bank: 'core_bank' | 'first_internet_bank' | 'grasshopper_bank'; closed_at: string; created_at: string; currency: 'USD'; entity_id: string; funding: 'loan' | 'deposits'; idempotency_key: string; informational_entity_id: string; interest_accrued: string; interest_accrued_at: string; interest_rate: string; loan: { credit_limit: number; grace_period_days: number; maturity_date: string; statement_day_of_month: number; statement_payment_type: 'balance' | 'interest_until_maturity'; }; name: string; program_id: string; status: 'closed' | 'open'; type: 'account'; }`\n  Accounts are your bank accounts with Increase. They store money, receive transfers, and send payments. They earn interest and have depository insurance.\n\n  - `id: string`\n  - `account_revenue_rate: string`\n  - `bank: 'core_bank' | 'first_internet_bank' | 'grasshopper_bank'`\n  - `closed_at: string`\n  - `created_at: string`\n  - `currency: 'USD'`\n  - `entity_id: string`\n  - `funding: 'loan' | 'deposits'`\n  - `idempotency_key: string`\n  - `informational_entity_id: string`\n  - `interest_accrued: string`\n  - `interest_accrued_at: string`\n  - `interest_rate: string`\n  - `loan: { credit_limit: number; grace_period_days: number; maturity_date: string; statement_day_of_month: number; statement_payment_type: 'balance' | 'interest_until_maturity'; }`\n  - `name: string`\n  - `program_id: string`\n  - `status: 'closed' | 'open'`\n  - `type: 'account'`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport YolkenIncreaseTest from 'yolken-increase-test';\n\nconst client = new YolkenIncreaseTest();\n\nconst account = await client.accounts.create({ name: 'New Account!' });\n\nconsole.log(account);\n```",
