    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.achPrenotifications.list(created_at?: { after?: string; before?: string; on_or_after?: string; on_or_before?: string; }, cursor?: string, idempotency_key?: string, limit?: number): { data: ach_prenotification[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n\n**get** `/ach_prenotifications`\n\nList ACH Prenotifications\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `created_at?: { after?: string; before?: string; on_or_after?: string; on_or_before?: string; }`\n  - `after?: string`\n    Return results after this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n  - `before?: string`\n    Return results before this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n  - `on_or_after?: string`\n    Return results on or after this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n  - `on_or_before?: string`\n    Return results on or before this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n\n- `cursor?: string`\n  Return the page of entries after this one.\n\n- `idempotency_key?: string`\n  Filter records to the one with the specified `idempotency_key` you chose for that object. This value is unique across Increase and is used to ensure that a request is only processed once. Learn more about [idempotency](https://increase.com/documentation/idempotency-keys).\n\n- `limit?: number`\n  Limit the size of the list that is returned. The default (and maximum) is 100 objects.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ data: { id: string; account_id: string; account_number: string; addendum: string; company_descriptive_date: string; company_discretionary_data: string; company_entry_description: string; company_name: string; created_at: string; credit_debit_indicator: 'credit' | 'debit'; effective_date: string; idempotency_key: string; individual_id: string; individual_name: string; notifications_of_change: object[]; prenotification_return: object; routing_number: string; standard_entry_class_code: string; status: 'pending_submitting' | 'requires_attention' | 'returned' | 'submitted'; type: 'ach_prenotification'; }[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n  A list of ACH Prenotification objects.\n\n  - `data: { id: string; account_id: string; account_number: string; addendum: string; company_descriptive_date: string; company_discretionary_data: string; company_entry_description: string; company_name: string; created_at: string; credit_debit_indicator: 'credit' | 'debit'; effective_date: string; idempotency_key: string; individual_id: string; individual_name: string; notifications_of_change: { change_code: string; corrected_data: string; created_at: string; }[]; prenotification_return: { created_at: string; return_reason_code: string; }; routing_number: string; standard_entry_class_code: string; status: 'pending_submitting' | 'requires_attention' | 'returned' | 'submitted'; type: 'ach_prenotification'; }[]`\n  - `next_cursor: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport YolkenIncreaseTest from 'yolken-increase-test';\n\nconst client = new YolkenIncreaseTest();\n\nconst achPrenotifications = await client.achPrenotifications.list();\n\nconsole.log(achPrenotifications);\n```",
