    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.achTransfers.list(account_id?: string, created_at?: { after?: string; before?: string; on_or_after?: string; on_or_before?: string; }, cursor?: string, external_account_id?: string, idempotency_key?: string, limit?: number, status?: { in?: string[]; }): { data: ach_transfer[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n\n**get** `/ach_transfers`\n\nList ACH Transfers\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `account_id?: string`\n  Filter ACH Transfers to those that originated from the specified Account.\n\n- `created_at?: { after?: string; before?: string; on_or_after?: string; on_or_before?: string; }`\n  - `after?: string`\n    Return results after this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n  - `before?: string`\n    Return results before this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n  - `on_or_after?: string`\n    Return results on or after this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n  - `on_or_before?: string`\n    Return results on or before this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n\n- `cursor?: string`\n  Return the page of entries after this one.\n\n- `external_account_id?: string`\n  Filter ACH Transfers to those made to the specified External Account.\n\n- `idempotency_key?: string`\n  Filter records to the one with the specified `idempotency_key` you chose for that object. This value is unique across Increase and is used to ensure that a request is only processed once. Learn more about [idempotency](https://increase.com/documentation/idempotency-keys).\n\n- `limit?: number`\n  Limit the size of the list that is returned. The default (and maximum) is 100 objects.\n\n- `status?: { in?: string[]; }`\n  - `in?: string[]`\n    Return results whose value is in the provided list. For GET requests, this should be encoded as a comma-delimited string, such as `?in=one,two,three`.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ data: { id: string; account_id: string; account_number: string; acknowledgement: object; addenda: object; amount: number; approval: object; cancellation: object; company_descriptive_date: string; company_discretionary_data: string; company_entry_description: string; company_id: string; company_name: string; created_at: string; created_by: object; currency: 'USD'; destination_account_holder: 'business' | 'individual' | 'unknown'; external_account_id: string; funding: 'checking' | 'savings' | 'general_ledger'; idempotency_key: string; inbound_funds_hold: inbound_funds_hold; individual_id: string; individual_name: string; network: 'ach'; notifications_of_change: object[]; pending_transaction_id: string; preferred_effective_date: object; return: object; routing_number: string; settlement: object; standard_entry_class_code: string; statement_descriptor: string; status: string; submission: object; transaction_id: string; type: 'ach_transfer'; }[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n  A list of ACH Transfer objects.\n\n  - `data: { id: string; account_id: string; account_number: string; acknowledgement: { acknowledged_at: string; }; addenda: { category: 'freeform' | 'payment_order_remittance_advice' | 'other'; freeform?: { entries: object[]; }; payment_order_remittance_advice?: { invoices: object[]; }; }; amount: number; approval: { approved_at: string; approved_by: string; }; cancellation: { canceled_at: string; canceled_by: string; }; company_descriptive_date: string; company_discretionary_data: string; company_entry_description: string; company_id: string; company_name: string; created_at: string; created_by: { category: 'api_key' | 'oauth_application' | 'user'; api_key?: { description: string; }; oauth_application?: { name: string; }; user?: { email: string; }; }; currency: 'USD'; destination_account_holder: 'business' | 'individual' | 'unknown'; external_account_id: string; funding: 'checking' | 'savings' | 'general_ledger'; idempotency_key: string; inbound_funds_hold: { amount: number; automatically_releases_at: string; created_at: string; currency: 'USD'; held_transaction_id: string; pending_transaction_id: string; released_at: string; status: 'held' | 'complete'; type: 'inbound_funds_hold'; }; individual_id: string; individual_name: string; network: 'ach'; notifications_of_change: { change_code: string; corrected_data: string; created_at: string; }[]; pending_transaction_id: string; preferred_effective_date: { date: string; settlement_schedule: 'same_day' | 'future_dated'; }; return: { created_at: string; raw_return_reason_code: string; return_reason_code: string; trace_number: string; transaction_id: string; transfer_id: string; }; routing_number: string; settlement: { settled_at: string; }; standard_entry_class_code: string; statement_descriptor: string; status: string; submission: { administrative_returns_expected_by: string; effective_date: string; expected_funds_settlement_at: string; expected_settlement_schedule: 'same_day' | 'future_dated'; submitted_at: string; trace_number: string; }; transaction_id: string; type: 'ach_transfer'; }[]`\n  - `next_cursor: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport YolkenIncreaseTest from 'yolken-increase-test';\n\nconst client = new YolkenIncreaseTest();\n\nconst achTransfers = await client.achTransfers.list();\n\nconsole.log(achTransfers);\n```",
