    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.bookkeepingAccounts.list(cursor?: string, idempotency_key?: string, limit?: number): { data: bookkeeping_account[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n\n**get** `/bookkeeping_accounts`\n\nList Bookkeeping Accounts\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `cursor?: string`\n  Return the page of entries after this one.\n\n- `idempotency_key?: string`\n  Filter records to the one with the specified `idempotency_key` you chose for that object. This value is unique across Increase and is used to ensure that a request is only processed once. Learn more about [idempotency](https://increase.com/documentation/idempotency-keys).\n\n- `limit?: number`\n  Limit the size of the list that is returned. The default (and maximum) is 100 objects.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ data: { id: string; account_id: string; compliance_category: 'commingled_cash' | 'customer_balance'; entity_id: string; idempotency_key: string; name: string; type: 'bookkeeping_account'; }[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n  A list of Bookkeeping Account objects.\n\n  - `data: { id: string; account_id: string; compliance_category: 'commingled_cash' | 'customer_balance'; entity_id: string; idempotency_key: string; name: string; type: 'bookkeeping_account'; }[]`\n  - `next_cursor: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport YolkenIncreaseTest from 'yolken-increase-test';\n\nconst client = new YolkenIncreaseTest();\n\nconst bookkeepingAccounts = await client.bookkeepingAccounts.list();\n\nconsole.log(bookkeepingAccounts);\n```",
