      "## list\n\n`client.cardDisputes.list(created_at?: { after?: string; before?: string; on_or_after?: string; on_or_before?: string; }, cursor?: string, idempotency_key?: string, limit?: number, status?: { in?: string[]; }): { data: card_dispute[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n\n**get** `/card_disputes`\n\nList Card Disputes\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `created_at?: { after?: string; before?: string; on_or_after?: string; on_or_before?: string; }`\n  - `after?: string`\n    Return results after this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n  - `before?: string`\n    Return results before this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n  - `on_or_after?: string`\n    Return results on or after this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n  - `on_or_before?: string`\n    Return results on or before this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n\n- `cursor?: string`\n  Return the page of entries after this one.\n\n- `idempotency_key?: string`\n  Filter records to the one with the specified `idempotency_key` you chose for that object. This value is unique across Increase and is used to ensure that a request is only processed once. Learn more about [idempotency](https://increase.com/documentation/idempotency-keys).\n\n- `limit?: number`\n  Limit the size of the list that is returned. The default (and maximum) is 100 objects.\n\n- `status?: { in?: string[]; }`\n  - `in?: string[]`\n    Filter Card Disputes for those with the specified status or statuses. For GET requests, this should be encoded as a comma-delimited string, such as `?in=one,two,three`.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ data: { id: string; amount: number; card_id: string; created_at: string; disputed_transaction_id: string; idempotency_key: string; loss: object; network: 'visa' | 'pulse'; status: string; type: 'card_dispute'; user_submission_required_by: string; visa: object; win: object; withdrawal: object; }[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n  A list of Card Dispute objects.\n\n  - `data: { id: string; amount: number; card_id: string; created_at: string; disputed_transaction_id: string; idempotency_key: string; loss: { lost_at: string; reason: 'user_withdrawn' | 'loss'; }; network: 'visa' | 'pulse'; status: string; type: 'card_dispute'; user_submission_required_by: string; visa: { network_events: { attachment_files: card_dispute_file_attachment[]; category: string; created_at: string; dispute_financial_transaction_id: string; chargeback_accepted?: object; chargeback_submitted?: object; chargeback_timed_out?: object; merchant_prearbitration_decline_submitted?: object; merchant_prearbitration_received?: object; merchant_prearbitration_timed_out?: object; represented?: object; representment_timed_out?: object; user_prearbitration_accepted?: object; user_prearbitration_declined?: object; user_prearbitration_submitted?: object; user_prearbitration_timed_out?: object; user_withdrawal_submitted?: object; }[]; required_user_submission_category: 'chargeback' | 'merchant_prearbitration_decline' | 'user_prearbitration'; user_submissions: { accepted_at: string; amount: number; attachment_files: card_dispute_file_attachment[]; category: 'chargeback' | 'merchant_prearbitration_decline' | 'user_prearbitration'; created_at: string; explanation: string; further_information_requested_at: string; further_information_requested_reason: string; status: 'abandoned' | 'accepted' | 'further_information_requested' | 'pending_reviewing'; updated_at: string; chargeback?: object; merchant_prearbitration_decline?: object; user_prearbitration?: object; }[]; }; win: { won_at: string; }; withdrawal: { explanation: string; }; }[]`\n  - `next_cursor: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport YolkenIncreaseTest from 'yolken-increase-test';\n\nconst client = new YolkenIncreaseTest();\n\nconst cardDisputes = await client.cardDisputes.list();\n\nconsole.log(cardDisputes);\n```",
