    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.entityBeneficialOwners.list(entity_id: string, cursor?: string, idempotency_key?: string, limit?: number): { data: beneficial_owner[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n\n**get** `/entity_beneficial_owners`\n\nList Beneficial Owners\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `entity_id: string`\n  The identifier of the Entity to list beneficial owners for. Only `corporation` entities have beneficial owners.\n\n- `cursor?: string`\n  Return the page of entries after this one.\n\n- `idempotency_key?: string`\n  Filter records to the one with the specified `idempotency_key` you chose for that object. This value is unique across Increase and is used to ensure that a request is only processed once. Learn more about [idempotency](https://increase.com/documentation/idempotency-keys).\n\n- `limit?: number`\n  Limit the size of the list that is returned. The default (and maximum) is 100 objects.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ data: { id: string; company_title: string; created_at: string; entity_id: string; idempotency_key: string; individual: object; prongs: 'ownership' | 'control'[]; type: 'entity_beneficial_owner'; }[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n  A list of Beneficial Owner objects.\n\n  - `data: { id: string; company_title: string; created_at: string; entity_id: string; idempotency_key: string; individual: { address: { city: string; country: string; line1: string; line2: string; state: string; zip: string; }; date_of_birth: string; identification: { method: string; number_last4: string; }; name: string; }; prongs: 'ownership' | 'control'[]; type: 'entity_beneficial_owner'; }[]`\n  - `next_cursor: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport YolkenIncreaseTest from 'yolken-increase-test';\n\nconst client = new YolkenIncreaseTest();\n\nconst entityBeneficialOwners = await client.entityBeneficialOwners.list({ entity_id: 'entity_id' });\n\nconsole.log(entityBeneficialOwners);\n```",
