    markdown:
      "## create\n\n`client.entityBeneficialOwners.create(entity_id: string, individual: { address: { city: string; country: string; line1: string; line2?: string; state?: string; zip?: string; }; date_of_birth: string; identification: { method: string; number: string; drivers_license?: object; other?: object; passport?: object; }; name: string; confirmed_no_us_tax_id?: boolean; }, prongs: 'ownership' | 'control'[], company_title?: string): { id: string; company_title: string; created_at: string; entity_id: string; idempotency_key: string; individual: object; prongs: 'ownership' | 'control'[]; type: 'entity_beneficial_owner'; }`\n\n**post** `/entity_beneficial_owners`\n\nCreate a beneficial owner\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `entity_id: string`\n  The identifier of the Entity to associate with the new Beneficial Owner.\n\n- `individual: { address: { city: string; country: string; line1: string; line2?: string; state?: string; zip?: string; }; date_of_birth: string; identification: { method: string; number: string; drivers_license?: { expiration_date: string; file_id: string; state: string; back_file_id?: string; }; other?: { country: string; description: string; file_id: string; back_file_id?: string; expiration_date?: string; }; passport?: { country: string; expiration_date: string; file_id: string; }; }; name: string; confirmed_no_us_tax_id?: boolean; }`\n  Personal details for the beneficial owner.\n  - `address: { city: string; country: string; line1: string; line2?: string; state?: string; zip?: string; }`\n    The individual's physical address. Mail receiving locations like PO Boxes and PMB's are disallowed.\n  - `date_of_birth: string`\n    The person's date of birth in YYYY-MM-DD format.\n  - `identification: { method: string; number: string; drivers_license?: { expiration_date: string; file_id: string; state: string; back_file_id?: string; }; other?: { country: string; description: string; file_id: string; back_file_id?: string; expiration_date?: string; }; passport?: { country: string; expiration_date: string; file_id: string; }; }`\n    A means of verifying the person's identity.\n  - `name: string`\n    The person's legal name.\n  - `confirmed_no_us_tax_id?: boolean`\n    The identification method for an individual can only be a passport, driver's license, or other document if you've confirmed the individual does not have a US tax id (either a Social Security Number or Individual Taxpayer Identification Number).\n\n- `prongs: 'ownership' | 'control'[]`\n  Why this person is considered a beneficial owner of the entity. At least one option is required, if a person is both a control person and owner, submit an array containing both.\n\n- `company_title?: string`\n  This person's role or title within the entity.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id: string; company_title: string; created_at: string; entity_id: string; idempotency_key: string; individual: { address: { city: string; country: string; line1: string; line2: string; state: string; zip: string; }; date_of_birth: string; identification: { method: string; number_last4: string; }; name: string; }; prongs: 'ownership' | 'control'[]; type: 'entity_beneficial_owner'; }`\n  Beneficial owners are the individuals who control or own 25% or more of a `corporation` entity. Beneficial owners are always people, and never organizations. Generally, you will need to submit between 1 and 5 beneficial owners for every `corporation` entity. You should update and archive beneficial owners for a corporation entity as their details change.\n\n  - `id: string`\n  - `company_title: string`\n  - `created_at: string`\n  - `entity_id: string`\n  - `idempotency_key: string`\n  - `individual: { address: { city: string; country: string; line1: string; line2: string; state: string; zip: string; }; date_of_birth: string; identification: { method: string; number_last4: string; }; name: string; }`\n  - `prongs: 'ownership' | 'control'[]`\n  - `type: 'entity_beneficial_owner'`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport YolkenIncreaseTest from 'yolken-increase-test';\n\nconst client = new YolkenIncreaseTest();\n\nconst beneficialOwner = await client.entityBeneficialOwners.create({\n  entity_id: 'entity_n8y8tnk2p9339ti393yi',\n  individual: {\n  address: {\n  city: 'New York',\n  country: 'US',\n  line1: '33 Liberty Street',\n},\n  date_of_birth: '1970-01-31',\n  identification: { method: 'social_security_number', number: '078051120' },\n  name: 'Ian Crease',\n},\n  prongs: ['control'],\n});\n\nconsole.log(beneficialOwner);\n```",
