    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.exports.list(category?: string, created_at?: { after?: string; before?: string; on_or_after?: string; on_or_before?: string; }, cursor?: string, form_1099_int?: { account_id?: string; }, form_1099_misc?: { account_id?: string; }, idempotency_key?: string, limit?: number, status?: { in?: 'pending' | 'complete' | 'failed'[]; }): { data: export[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n\n**get** `/exports`\n\nList Exports\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `category?: string`\n  Filter Exports for those with the specified category.\n\n- `account_statement_ofx` - Export an Open Financial Exchange (OFX) file of transactions and balances for a given time range and Account.\n- `account_statement_bai2` - Export a BAI2 file of transactions and balances for a given date and optional Account.\n- `transaction_csv` - Export a CSV of all transactions for a given time range.\n- `balance_csv` - Export a CSV of account balances for the dates in a given range.\n- `bookkeeping_account_balance_csv` - Export a CSV of bookkeeping account balances for the dates in a given range.\n- `entity_csv` - Export a CSV of entities with a given status.\n- `vendor_csv` - Export a CSV of vendors added to the third-party risk management dashboard.\n- `dashboard_table_csv` - Certain dashboard tables are available as CSV exports. This export cannot be created via the API.\n- `account_verification_letter` - A PDF of an account verification letter.\n- `funding_instructions` - A PDF of funding instructions.\n- `form_1099_int` - A PDF of an Internal Revenue Service Form 1099-INT.\n- `form_1099_misc` - A PDF of an Internal Revenue Service Form 1099-MISC.\n- `fee_csv` - Export a CSV of fees. The time range must not include any fees that are part of an open fee statement.\n- `voided_check` - A PDF of a voided check.\n\n- `created_at?: { after?: string; before?: string; on_or_after?: string; on_or_before?: string; }`\n  - `after?: string`\n    Return results after this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n  - `before?: string`\n    Return results before this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n  - `on_or_after?: string`\n    Return results on or after this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n  - `on_or_before?: string`\n    Return results on or before this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n\n- `cursor?: string`\n  Return the page of entries after this one.\n\n- `form_1099_int?: { account_id?: string; }`\n  - `account_id?: string`\n    Filter Form 1099-INT Exports to those for the specified Account.\n\n- `form_1099_misc?: { account_id?: string; }`\n  - `account_id?: string`\n    Filter Form 1099-MISC Exports to those for the specified Account.\n\n- `idempotency_key?: string`\n  Filter records to the one with the specified `idempotency_key` you chose for that object. This value is unique across Increase and is used to ensure that a request is only processed once. Learn more about [idempotency](https://increase.com/documentation/idempotency-keys).\n\n- `limit?: number`\n  Limit the size of the list that is returned. The default (and maximum) is 100 objects.\n\n- `status?: { in?: 'pending' | 'complete' | 'failed'[]; }`\n  - `in?: 'pending' | 'complete' | 'failed'[]`\n    Filter Exports for those with the specified status or statuses. For GET requests, this should be encoded as a comma-delimited string, such as `?in=one,two,three`.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ data: { id: string; account_statement_bai2: object; account_statement_ofx: object; account_verification_letter: object; balance_csv: object; bookkeeping_account_balance_csv: object; category: string; created_at: string; dashboard_table_csv: object; entity_csv: object; fee_csv: object; form_1099_int: object; form_1099_misc: object; funding_instructions: object; idempotency_key: string; result: object; status: 'pending' | 'complete' | 'failed'; transaction_csv: object; type: 'export'; vendor_csv: object; voided_check: object; }[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n  A list of Export objects.\n\n  - `data: { id: string; account_statement_bai2: { account_id: string; effective_date: string; program_id: string; }; account_statement_ofx: { account_id: string; created_at: { after: string; before: string; }; }; account_verification_letter: { account_number_id: string; balance_date: string; }; balance_csv: { account_id: string; created_at: { after: string; before: string; }; }; bookkeeping_account_balance_csv: { bookkeeping_account_id: string; created_at: { after: string; before: string; }; }; category: string; created_at: string; dashboard_table_csv: object; entity_csv: object; fee_csv: { created_at: { after: string; before: string; }; }; form_1099_int: { account_id: string; corrected: boolean; description: string; year: number; }; form_1099_misc: { account_id: string; corrected: boolean; year: number; }; funding_instructions: { account_number_id: string; }; idempotency_key: string; result: { file_id: string; }; status: 'pending' | 'complete' | 'failed'; transaction_csv: { account_id: string; created_at: { after: string; before: string; }; }; type: 'export'; vendor_csv: object; voided_check: { account_number_id: string; payer: { line: string; }[]; }; }[]`\n  - `next_cursor: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport YolkenIncreaseTest from 'yolken-increase-test';\n\nconst client = new YolkenIncreaseTest();\n\nconst exports = await client.exports.list();\n\nconsole.log(exports);\n```",
