    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.externalAccounts.list(cursor?: string, idempotency_key?: string, limit?: number, routing_number?: string, status?: { in?: 'active' | 'archived'[]; }): { data: external_account[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n\n**get** `/external_accounts`\n\nList External Accounts\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `cursor?: string`\n  Return the page of entries after this one.\n\n- `idempotency_key?: string`\n  Filter records to the one with the specified `idempotency_key` you chose for that object. This value is unique across Increase and is used to ensure that a request is only processed once. Learn more about [idempotency](https://increase.com/documentation/idempotency-keys).\n\n- `limit?: number`\n  Limit the size of the list that is returned. The default (and maximum) is 100 objects.\n\n- `routing_number?: string`\n  Filter External Accounts to those with the specified Routing Number.\n\n- `status?: { in?: 'active' | 'archived'[]; }`\n  - `in?: 'active' | 'archived'[]`\n    Filter External Accounts for those with the specified status or statuses. For GET requests, this should be encoded as a comma-delimited string, such as `?in=one,two,three`.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ data: { id: string; account_holder: 'business' | 'individual' | 'unknown'; account_number: string; created_at: string; description: string; funding: 'checking' | 'savings' | 'general_ledger' | 'other'; idempotency_key: string; routing_number: string; status: 'active' | 'archived'; type: 'external_account'; }[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n  A list of External Account objects.\n\n  - `data: { id: string; account_holder: 'business' | 'individual' | 'unknown'; account_number: string; created_at: string; description: string; funding: 'checking' | 'savings' | 'general_ledger' | 'other'; idempotency_key: string; routing_number: string; status: 'active' | 'archived'; type: 'external_account'; }[]`\n  - `next_cursor: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport YolkenIncreaseTest from 'yolken-increase-test';\n\nconst client = new YolkenIncreaseTest();\n\nconst externalAccounts = await client.externalAccounts.list();\n\nconsole.log(externalAccounts);\n```",
