    markdown:
      "## create\n\n`client.fednowTransfers.create(amount: number, creditor_name: string, debtor_name: string, source_account_number_id: string, unstructured_remittance_information: string, account_number?: string, creditor_address?: { city: string; postal_code: string; state: string; line1?: string; }, debtor_address?: { city: string; postal_code: string; state: string; line1?: string; }, external_account_id?: string, require_approval?: boolean, routing_number?: string): { id: string; account_id: string; account_number: string; acknowledgement: object; amount: number; created_at: string; created_by: object; creditor_address: object; creditor_name: string; currency: 'USD'; debtor_name: string; external_account_id: string; idempotency_key: string; pending_transaction_id: string; rejection: object; routing_number: string; source_account_number_id: string; status: string; submission: object; transaction_id: string; type: 'fednow_transfer'; unique_end_to_end_transaction_reference: string; unstructured_remittance_information: string; }`\n\n**post** `/fednow_transfers`\n\nCreate a FedNow Transfer\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `amount: number`\n  The amount, in minor units, to send to the creditor.\n\n- `creditor_name: string`\n  The creditor's name.\n\n- `debtor_name: string`\n  The debtor's name.\n\n- `source_account_number_id: string`\n  The Account Number to include in the transfer as the debtor's account number.\n\n- `unstructured_remittance_information: string`\n  Unstructured remittance information to include in the transfer.\n\n- `account_number?: string`\n  The creditor's account number.\n\n- `creditor_address?: { city: string; postal_code: string; state: string; line1?: string; }`\n  The creditor's address.\n  - `city: string`\n    The city, district, town, or village of the address.\n  - `postal_code: string`\n    The postal code component of the address.\n  - `state: string`\n    The US state component of the address.\n  - `line1?: string`\n    The first line of the address. This is usually the street number and street.\n\n- `debtor_address?: { city: string; postal_code: string; state: string; line1?: string; }`\n  The debtor's address.\n  - `city: string`\n    The city, district, town, or village of the address.\n  - `postal_code: string`\n    The postal code component of the address.\n  - `state: string`\n    The US state component of the address.\n  - `line1?: string`\n    The first line of the address. This is usually the street number and street.\n\n- `external_account_id?: string`\n  The ID of an External Account to initiate a transfer to. If this parameter is provided, `account_number` and `routing_number` must be absent.\n\n- `require_approval?: boolean`\n  Whether the transfer requires explicit approval via the dashboard or API.\n\n- `routing_number?: string`\n  The creditor's bank account routing number.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id: string; account_id: string; account_number: string; acknowledgement: { acknowledged_at: string; }; amount: number; created_at: string; created_by: { category: 'api_key' | 'oauth_application' | 'user'; api_key?: { description: string; }; oauth_application?: { name: string; }; user?: { email: string; }; }; creditor_address: { city: string; line1: string; postal_code: string; state: string; }; creditor_name: string; currency: 'USD'; debtor_name: string; external_account_id: string; idempotency_key: string; pending_transaction_id: string; rejection: { reject_reason_additional_information: string; reject_reason_code: string; rejected_at: string; }; routing_number: string; source_account_number_id: string; status: string; submission: { message_identification: string; submitted_at: string; }; transaction_id: string; type: 'fednow_transfer'; unique_end_to_end_transaction_reference: string; unstructured_remittance_information: string; }`\n  FedNow transfers move funds, within seconds, between your Increase account and any other account supporting FedNow.\n\n  - `id: string`\n  - `account_id: string`\n  - `account_number: string`\n  - `acknowledgement: { acknowledged_at: string; }`\n  - `amount: number`\n  - `created_at: string`\n  - `created_by: { category: 'api_key' | 'oauth_application' | 'user'; api_key?: { description: string; }; oauth_application?: { name: string; }; user?: { email: string; }; }`\n  - `creditor_address: { city: string; line1: string; postal_code: string; state: string; }`\n  - `creditor_name: string`\n  - `currency: 'USD'`\n  - `debtor_name: string`\n  - `external_account_id: string`\n  - `idempotency_key: string`\n  - `pending_transaction_id: string`\n  - `rejection: { reject_reason_additional_information: string; reject_reason_code: string; rejected_at: string; }`\n  - `routing_number: string`\n  - `source_account_number_id: string`\n  - `status: string`\n  - `submission: { message_identification: string; submitted_at: string; }`\n  - `transaction_id: string`\n  - `type: 'fednow_transfer'`\n  - `unique_end_to_end_transaction_reference: string`\n  - `unstructured_remittance_information: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport YolkenIncreaseTest from 'yolken-increase-test';\n\nconst client = new YolkenIncreaseTest();\n\nconst fednowTransfer = await client.fednowTransfers.create({\n  amount: 100,\n  creditor_name: 'Ian Crease',\n  debtor_name: 'National Phonograph Company',\n  source_account_number_id: 'account_number_v18nkfqm6afpsrvy82b2',\n  unstructured_remittance_information: 'Invoice 29582',\n});\n\nconsole.log(fednowTransfer);\n```",
