      "## create\n\n`client.physicalCards.create(card_id: string, cardholder: { first_name: string; last_name: string; }, shipment: { address: { city: string; line1: string; name: string; postal_code: string; state: string; country?: string; line2?: string; line3?: string; phone_number?: string; }; method: 'usps' | 'fedex_priority_overnight' | 'fedex_2_day' | 'dhl_worldwide_express'; schedule?: 'next_day' | 'same_day'; }, physical_card_profile_id?: string): { id: string; card_id: string; cardholder: object; created_at: string; idempotency_key: string; physical_card_profile_id: string; shipment: object; status: 'active' | 'disabled' | 'canceled'; type: 'physical_card'; }`\n\n**post** `/physical_cards`\n\nCreate a Physical Card\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `card_id: string`\n  The underlying card representing this physical card.\n\n- `cardholder: { first_name: string; last_name: string; }`\n  Details about the cardholder, as it will appear on the physical card.\n  - `first_name: string`\n    The cardholder's first name.\n  - `last_name: string`\n    The cardholder's last name.\n\n- `shipment: { address: { city: string; line1: string; name: string; postal_code: string; state: string; country?: string; line2?: string; line3?: string; phone_number?: string; }; method: 'usps' | 'fedex_priority_overnight' | 'fedex_2_day' | 'dhl_worldwide_express'; schedule?: 'next_day' | 'same_day'; }`\n  The details used to ship this physical card.\n  - `address: { city: string; line1: string; name: string; postal_code: string; state: string; country?: string; line2?: string; line3?: string; phone_number?: string; }`\n    The address to where the card should be shipped.\n  - `method: 'usps' | 'fedex_priority_overnight' | 'fedex_2_day' | 'dhl_worldwide_express'`\n    The shipping method to use.\n\n- `usps` - USPS Post.\n- `fedex_priority_overnight` - FedEx Priority Overnight, no signature.\n- `fedex_2_day` - FedEx 2-day.\n- `dhl_worldwide_express` - DHL Worldwide Express, international shipping only.\n  - `schedule?: 'next_day' | 'same_day'`\n    When this physical card should be produced by the card printer. The default timeline is the day after the card printer receives the order, except for `FEDEX_PRIORITY_OVERNIGHT` cards, which default to `SAME_DAY`. To use faster production methods, please reach out to [support@increase.com](mailto:support@increase.com).\n\n- `next_day` - The physical card will be shipped one business day after the order is received by the card printer. A card that is submitted to Increase on a Monday evening (Pacific Time) will ship out on Wednesday.\n- `same_day` - The physical card will be shipped on the same business day that the order is received by the card printer. A card that is submitted to Increase on a Monday evening (Pacific Time) will ship out on Tuesday.\n\n- `physical_card_profile_id?: string`\n  The physical card profile to use for this physical card. The latest default physical card profile will be used if not provided.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id: string; card_id: string; cardholder: { first_name: string; last_name: string; }; created_at: string; idempotency_key: string; physical_card_profile_id: string; shipment: { address: { city: string; country: string; line1: string; line2: string; line3: string; name: string; postal_code: string; state: string; }; method: 'usps' | 'fedex_priority_overnight' | 'fedex_2_day' | 'dhl_worldwide_express'; schedule: 'next_day' | 'same_day'; status: string; tracking: { number: string; return_number: string; return_reason: string; shipped_at: string; updates: object[]; }; }; status: 'active' | 'disabled' | 'canceled'; type: 'physical_card'; }`\n  Custom physical Visa cards that are shipped to your customers. The artwork is configurable by a connected [Card Profile](/documentation/api#card-profiles). The same Card can be used for multiple Physical Cards. Printing cards incurs a fee. Please contact [support@increase.com](mailto:support@increase.com) for pricing!\n\n  - `id: string`\n  - `card_id: string`\n  - `cardholder: { first_name: string; last_name: string; }`\n  - `created_at: string`\n  - `idempotency_key: string`\n  - `physical_card_profile_id: string`\n  - `shipment: { address: { city: string; country: string; line1: string; line2: string; line3: string; name: string; postal_code: string; state: string; }; method: 'usps' | 'fedex_priority_overnight' | 'fedex_2_day' | 'dhl_worldwide_express'; schedule: 'next_day' | 'same_day'; status: string; tracking: { number: string; return_number: string; return_reason: string; shipped_at: string; updates: { carrier_estimated_delivery_at: string; category: 'in_transit' | 'processed_for_delivery' | 'delivered' | 'delivery_issue' | 'returned_to_sender'; city: string; created_at: string; postal_code: string; state: string; }[]; }; }`\n  - `status: 'active' | 'disabled' | 'canceled'`\n  - `type: 'physical_card'`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport YolkenIncreaseTest from 'yolken-increase-test';\n\nconst client = new YolkenIncreaseTest();\n\nconst physicalCard = await client.physicalCards.create({\n  card_id: 'card_oubs0hwk5rn6knuecxg2',\n  cardholder: { first_name: 'Ian', last_name: 'Crease' },\n  shipment: {\n  address: {\n  city: 'New York',\n  line1: '33 Liberty Street',\n  name: 'Ian Crease',\n  postal_code: '10045',\n  state: 'NY',\n},\n  method: 'usps',\n},\n});\n\nconsole.log(physicalCard);\n```",
