    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.realTimePaymentsTransfers.list(account_id?: string, created_at?: { after?: string; before?: string; on_or_after?: string; on_or_before?: string; }, cursor?: string, external_account_id?: string, idempotency_key?: string, limit?: number, status?: { in?: string[]; }): { data: transfer[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n\n**get** `/real_time_payments_transfers`\n\nList Real-Time Payments Transfers\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `account_id?: string`\n  Filter Real-Time Payments Transfers to those belonging to the specified Account.\n\n- `created_at?: { after?: string; before?: string; on_or_after?: string; on_or_before?: string; }`\n  - `after?: string`\n    Return results after this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n  - `before?: string`\n    Return results before this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n  - `on_or_after?: string`\n    Return results on or after this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n  - `on_or_before?: string`\n    Return results on or before this [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) timestamp.\n\n- `cursor?: string`\n  Return the page of entries after this one.\n\n- `external_account_id?: string`\n  Filter Real-Time Payments Transfers to those made to the specified External Account.\n\n- `idempotency_key?: string`\n  Filter records to the one with the specified `idempotency_key` you chose for that object. This value is unique across Increase and is used to ensure that a request is only processed once. Learn more about [idempotency](https://increase.com/documentation/idempotency-keys).\n\n- `limit?: number`\n  Limit the size of the list that is returned. The default (and maximum) is 100 objects.\n\n- `status?: { in?: string[]; }`\n  - `in?: string[]`\n    Return results whose value is in the provided list. For GET requests, this should be encoded as a comma-delimited string, such as `?in=one,two,three`.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ data: { id: string; account_id: string; account_number: string; acknowledgement: object; amount: number; approval: object; cancellation: object; created_at: string; created_by: object; creditor_name: string; currency: 'USD'; debtor_name: string; external_account_id: string; idempotency_key: string; pending_transaction_id: string; rejection: object; routing_number: string; source_account_number_id: string; status: string; submission: object; transaction_id: string; type: 'real_time_payments_transfer'; ultimate_creditor_name: string; ultimate_debtor_name: string; unstructured_remittance_information: string; }[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n  A list of Real-Time Payments Transfer objects.\n\n  - `data: { id: string; account_id: string; account_number: string; acknowledgement: { acknowledged_at: string; }; amount: number; approval: { approved_at: string; approved_by: string; }; cancellation: { canceled_at: string; canceled_by: string; }; created_at: string; created_by: { category: 'api_key' | 'oauth_application' | 'user'; api_key?: { description: string; }; oauth_application?: { name: string; }; user?: { email: string; }; }; creditor_name: string; currency: 'USD'; debtor_name: string; external_account_id: string; idempotency_key: string; pending_transaction_id: string; rejection: { reject_reason_additional_information: string; reject_reason_code: string; rejected_at: string; }; routing_number: string; source_account_number_id: string; status: string; submission: { submitted_at: string; transaction_identification: string; }; transaction_id: string; type: 'real_time_payments_transfer'; ultimate_creditor_name: string; ultimate_debtor_name: string; unstructured_remittance_information: string; }[]`\n  - `next_cursor: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport YolkenIncreaseTest from 'yolken-increase-test';\n\nconst client = new YolkenIncreaseTest();\n\nconst realTimePaymentsTransfers = await client.realTimePaymentsTransfers.list();\n\nconsole.log(realTimePaymentsTransfers);\n```",
