    description:
      'You can use this API to confirm if a routing number is valid, such as when a user is providing you with bank account details. Since routing numbers uniquely identify a bank, this will always return 0 or 1 entry. In Sandbox, the only valid routing number for this method is 110000000.',
    stainlessPath: '(resource) routing_numbers > (method) list',
    qualified: 'client.routingNumbers.list',
    params: ['routing_number: string;', 'cursor?: string;', 'limit?: number;'],
    response:
      "{ data: { ach_transfers: 'supported' | 'not_supported'; fednow_transfers: 'supported' | 'not_supported'; name: string; real_time_payments_transfers: 'supported' | 'not_supported'; routing_number: string; type: 'routing_number'; wire_transfers: 'supported' | 'not_supported'; }[]; next_cursor: string; }",
    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.routingNumbers.list(routing_number: string, cursor?: string, limit?: number): { data: object[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n\n**get** `/routing_numbers`\n\nYou can use this API to confirm if a routing number is valid, such as when a user is providing you with bank account details. Since routing numbers uniquely identify a bank, this will always return 0 or 1 entry. In Sandbox, the only valid routing number for this method is 110000000.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `routing_number: string`\n  Filter financial institutions by routing number.\n\n- `cursor?: string`\n  Return the page of entries after this one.\n\n- `limit?: number`\n  Limit the size of the list that is returned. The default (and maximum) is 100 objects.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ data: { ach_transfers: 'supported' | 'not_supported'; fednow_transfers: 'supported' | 'not_supported'; name: string; real_time_payments_transfers: 'supported' | 'not_supported'; routing_number: string; type: 'routing_number'; wire_transfers: 'supported' | 'not_supported'; }[]; next_cursor: string; }`\n  A list of Routing Number objects.\n\n  - `data: { ach_transfers: 'supported' | 'not_supported'; fednow_transfers: 'supported' | 'not_supported'; name: string; real_time_payments_transfers: 'supported' | 'not_supported'; routing_number: string; type: 'routing_number'; wire_transfers: 'supported' | 'not_supported'; }[]`\n  - `next_cursor: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport YolkenIncreaseTest from 'yolken-increase-test';\n\nconst client = new YolkenIncreaseTest();\n\nconst routingNumbers = await client.routingNumbers.list({ routing_number: 'xxxxxxxxx' });\n\nconsole.log(routingNumbers);\n```",
