    markdown:
      "## create_account_statement\n\n`client.simulations.createAccountStatement(account_id: string): { id: string; account_id: string; created_at: string; ending_balance: number; file_id: string; loan: object; starting_balance: number; statement_period_end: string; statement_period_start: string; type: 'account_statement'; }`\n\n**post** `/simulations/account_statements`\n\nSimulates an [Account Statement](#account-statements) being created for an account. In production, Account Statements are generated once per month.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `account_id: string`\n  The identifier of the Account the statement is for.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id: string; account_id: string; created_at: string; ending_balance: number; file_id: string; loan: { due_at: string; due_balance: number; past_due_balance: number; }; starting_balance: number; statement_period_end: string; statement_period_start: string; type: 'account_statement'; }`\n  Account Statements are generated monthly for every active Account. You can access the statement's data via the API or retrieve a PDF with its details via its associated File.\n\n  - `id: string`\n  - `account_id: string`\n  - `created_at: string`\n  - `ending_balance: number`\n  - `file_id: string`\n  - `loan: { due_at: string; due_balance: number; past_due_balance: number; }`\n  - `starting_balance: number`\n  - `statement_period_end: string`\n  - `statement_period_start: string`\n  - `type: 'account_statement'`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport YolkenIncreaseTest from 'yolken-increase-test';\n\nconst client = new YolkenIncreaseTest();\n\nconst accountStatement = await client.simulations.createAccountStatement({ account_id: 'account_in71c4amph0vgo2qllky' });\n\nconsole.log(accountStatement);\n```",
