    markdown:
      "## refuse\n\n`client.simulations.wireDrawdownRequests.refuse(wire_drawdown_request_id: string): { id: string; account_number_id: string; amount: number; created_at: string; creditor_address: object; creditor_name: string; currency: string; debtor_account_number: string; debtor_address: object; debtor_external_account_id: string; debtor_name: string; debtor_routing_number: string; fulfillment_inbound_wire_transfer_id: string; idempotency_key: string; status: 'pending_submission' | 'fulfilled' | 'pending_response' | 'refused'; submission: object; type: 'wire_drawdown_request'; unstructured_remittance_information: string; }`\n\n**post** `/simulations/wire_drawdown_requests/{wire_drawdown_request_id}/refuse`\n\nSimulates a Wire Drawdown Request being refused by the debtor.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `wire_drawdown_request_id: string`\n  The identifier of the Wire Drawdown Request you wish to refuse.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id: string; account_number_id: string; amount: number; created_at: string; creditor_address: { city: string; country: string; line1: string; line2: string; postal_code: string; state: string; }; creditor_name: string; currency: string; debtor_account_number: string; debtor_address: { city: string; country: string; line1: string; line2: string; postal_code: string; state: string; }; debtor_external_account_id: string; debtor_name: string; debtor_routing_number: string; fulfillment_inbound_wire_transfer_id: string; idempotency_key: string; status: 'pending_submission' | 'fulfilled' | 'pending_response' | 'refused'; submission: { input_message_accountability_data: string; }; type: 'wire_drawdown_request'; unstructured_remittance_information: string; }`\n  Wire drawdown requests enable you to request that someone else send you a wire. Because there is nuance to making sure your counterparty's bank processes these correctly, we ask that you reach out to [support@increase.com](mailto:support@increase.com) to enable this feature so we can help you plan your integration. For more information, see our [Wire Drawdown Requests documentation](/documentation/wire-drawdown-requests).\n\n  - `id: string`\n  - `account_number_id: string`\n  - `amount: number`\n  - `created_at: string`\n  - `creditor_address: { city: string; country: string; line1: string; line2: string; postal_code: string; state: string; }`\n  - `creditor_name: string`\n  - `currency: string`\n  - `debtor_account_number: string`\n  - `debtor_address: { city: string; country: string; line1: string; line2: string; postal_code: string; state: string; }`\n  - `debtor_external_account_id: string`\n  - `debtor_name: string`\n  - `debtor_routing_number: string`\n  - `fulfillment_inbound_wire_transfer_id: string`\n  - `idempotency_key: string`\n  - `status: 'pending_submission' | 'fulfilled' | 'pending_response' | 'refused'`\n  - `submission: { input_message_accountability_data: string; }`\n  - `type: 'wire_drawdown_request'`\n  - `unstructured_remittance_information: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport YolkenIncreaseTest from 'yolken-increase-test';\n\nconst client = new YolkenIncreaseTest();\n\nconst wireDrawdownRequest = await client.simulations.wireDrawdownRequests.refuse('wire_drawdown_request_q6lmocus3glo0lr2bfv3');\n\nconsole.log(wireDrawdownRequest);\n```",
