    markdown:
      "## create\n\n`client.wireTransfers.create(account_id: string, amount: number, creditor: { name: string; address?: { unstructured: object; }; }, remittance: { category: 'unstructured' | 'tax'; tax?: { date: string; identification_number: string; type_code: string; }; unstructured?: { message: string; }; }, account_number?: string, debtor?: { name: string; address?: { unstructured: object; }; }, external_account_id?: string, inbound_wire_drawdown_request_id?: string, require_approval?: boolean, routing_number?: string, source_account_number_id?: string): { id: string; account_id: string; account_number: string; amount: number; approval: object; cancellation: object; created_at: string; created_by: object; creditor: object; currency: 'USD'; debtor: object; external_account_id: string; idempotency_key: string; inbound_wire_drawdown_request_id: string; network: 'wire'; pending_transaction_id: string; remittance: object; reversal: object; routing_number: string; source_account_number_id: string; status: string; submission: object; transaction_id: string; type: 'wire_transfer'; }`\n\n**post** `/wire_transfers`\n\nCreate a Wire Transfer\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `account_id: string`\n  The identifier for the account that will send the transfer.\n\n- `amount: number`\n  The transfer amount in USD cents.\n\n- `creditor: { name: string; address?: { unstructured: { line1: string; line2?: string; line3?: string; }; }; }`\n  The person or business that is receiving the funds from the transfer.\n  - `name: string`\n    The person or business's name.\n  - `address?: { unstructured: { line1: string; line2?: string; line3?: string; }; }`\n    The person or business's address.\n\n- `remittance: { category: 'unstructured' | 'tax'; tax?: { date: string; identification_number: string; type_code: string; }; unstructured?: { message: string; }; }`\n  Additional remittance information related to the wire transfer.\n  - `category: 'unstructured' | 'tax'`\n    The type of remittance information being passed.\n\n- `unstructured` - The wire transfer contains unstructured remittance information.\n- `tax` - The wire transfer is for tax payment purposes to the Internal Revenue Service (IRS).\n  - `tax?: { date: string; identification_number: string; type_code: string; }`\n    Internal Revenue Service (IRS) tax repayment information. Required if `category` is equal to `tax`.\n  - `unstructured?: { message: string; }`\n    Unstructured remittance information. Required if `category` is equal to `unstructured`.\n\n- `account_number?: string`\n  The account number for the destination account.\n\n- `debtor?: { name: string; address?: { unstructured: { line1: string; line2?: string; line3?: string; }; }; }`\n  The person or business whose funds are being transferred. This is only necessary if you're transferring from a commingled account. Otherwise, we'll use the associated entity's details.\n  - `name: string`\n    The person or business's name.\n  - `address?: { unstructured: { line1: string; line2?: string; line3?: string; }; }`\n    The person or business's address.\n\n- `external_account_id?: string`\n  The ID of an External Account to initiate a transfer to. If this parameter is provided, `account_number` and `routing_number` must be absent.\n\n- `inbound_wire_drawdown_request_id?: string`\n  The ID of an Inbound Wire Drawdown Request in response to which this transfer is being sent.\n\n- `require_approval?: boolean`\n  Whether the transfer requires explicit approval via the dashboard or API.\n\n- `routing_number?: string`\n  The American Bankers' Association (ABA) Routing Transit Number (RTN) for the destination account.\n\n- `source_account_number_id?: string`\n  The ID of an Account Number that will be passed to the wire's recipient\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id: string; account_id: string; account_number: string; amount: number; approval: { approved_at: string; approved_by: string; }; cancellation: { canceled_at: string; canceled_by: string; }; created_at: string; created_by: { category: 'api_key' | 'oauth_application' | 'user'; api_key?: { description: string; }; oauth_application?: { name: string; }; user?: { email: string; }; }; creditor: { address: { unstructured: object; }; name: string; }; currency: 'USD'; debtor: { address: { unstructured: object; }; name: string; }; external_account_id: string; idempotency_key: string; inbound_wire_drawdown_request_id: string; network: 'wire'; pending_transaction_id: string; remittance: { category: 'unstructured' | 'tax'; tax?: { date: string; identification_number: string; type_code: string; }; unstructured?: { message: string; }; }; reversal: { amount: number; created_at: string; debtor_routing_number: string; description: string; input_cycle_date: string; input_message_accountability_data: string; input_sequence_number: string; input_source: string; instruction_identification: string; return_reason_additional_information: string; return_reason_code: string; return_reason_code_description: string; transaction_id: string; wire_transfer_id: string; }; routing_number: string; source_account_number_id: string; status: string; submission: { input_message_accountability_data: string; submitted_at: string; }; transaction_id: string; type: 'wire_transfer'; }`\n  Wire transfers move funds between your Increase account and any other account accessible by Fedwire.\n\n  - `id: string`\n  - `account_id: string`\n  - `account_number: string`\n  - `amount: number`\n  - `approval: { approved_at: string; approved_by: string; }`\n  - `cancellation: { canceled_at: string; canceled_by: string; }`\n  - `created_at: string`\n  - `created_by: { category: 'api_key' | 'oauth_application' | 'user'; api_key?: { description: string; }; oauth_application?: { name: string; }; user?: { email: string; }; }`\n  - `creditor: { address: { unstructured: { line1: string; line2: string; line3: string; }; }; name: string; }`\n  - `currency: 'USD'`\n  - `debtor: { address: { unstructured: { line1: string; line2: string; line3: string; }; }; name: string; }`\n  - `external_account_id: string`\n  - `idempotency_key: string`\n  - `inbound_wire_drawdown_request_id: string`\n  - `network: 'wire'`\n  - `pending_transaction_id: string`\n  - `remittance: { category: 'unstructured' | 'tax'; tax?: { date: string; identification_number: string; type_code: string; }; unstructured?: { message: string; }; }`\n  - `reversal: { amount: number; created_at: string; debtor_routing_number: string; description: string; input_cycle_date: string; input_message_accountability_data: string; input_sequence_number: string; input_source: string; instruction_identification: string; return_reason_additional_information: string; return_reason_code: string; return_reason_code_description: string; transaction_id: string; wire_transfer_id: string; }`\n  - `routing_number: string`\n  - `source_account_number_id: string`\n  - `status: string`\n  - `submission: { input_message_accountability_data: string; submitted_at: string; }`\n  - `transaction_id: string`\n  - `type: 'wire_transfer'`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport YolkenIncreaseTest from 'yolken-increase-test';\n\nconst client = new YolkenIncreaseTest();\n\nconst wireTransfer = await client.wireTransfers.create({\n  account_id: 'account_in71c4amph0vgo2qllky',\n  amount: 100,\n  creditor: { name: 'Ian Crease' },\n  remittance: { category: 'unstructured' },\n});\n\nconsole.log(wireTransfer);\n```",
